WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.300
This is Priya. She just walked out of a
Friday night show.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.500
One tap turns that night
into a ticket stub.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.900
Every film prints its own stub, and her
diary fills with posters.

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.700
Rewatches, tags, notes, the watchlist:
it all lives on her phone.

5
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.700
34,000 titles are already on the phone.

6
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.950
Offline, no signal needed.

7
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.450
Search forgives spaces and punctuation,

8
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.100
and knows actors and directors.

9
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.400
Streaming services sit on every film page,
straight from Wikipedia.

10
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.900
Stats for any month: hyphen, slash,

11
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.000
films, rupees, first-day-first-shows.

12
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.500
Tap a bar to see the films behind it,
then share the night.

13
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.400
Signing in is optional.

14
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.400
Signed in, her diary follows
her everywhere.

15
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.300
Friends' shelves, a taste-match score,

16
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.000
and a feed of what they watch.

17
00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.900
One tap adds to the watchlist,

18
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.000
one tap sends a reaction.

19
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.100
Everyone in the group swipes:

20
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.400
right to watch, up if they've seen it.

21
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.900
The poll picks the night.

22
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.000
One tap writes every stub.

23
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.900
Talkies. Every night becomes a ticket.
